## The stories

**Read this one:**

- **Abigail Haddad**: She built a small site in a couple of evenings, shared it at meetups and online, and found the contract work she wanted. [Make Things, Tell People](https://presentofcoding.substack.com/p/make-things-tell-people), The Present of Coding, 2025

**Then choose one of these:**

- **Dean Levinson**: As a high-school student, he built a fix for his classroom's video problem. The company behind the system hired him. [EdSurge, 2019](https://www.edsurge.com/news/2019-03-04-a-student-improved-a-classroom-tech-solution-so-the-company-hired-him)
- **Kareem Abukhadra**: Told there were no roles, he asked a VP about his problems for 20 minutes. The VP created an internship for him. [6 months of failure, 2020](https://kareemabukhadra.substack.com/p/6-months-of-failure)
- **Katie Brown**: Her team won Splunk's security competition on tools she had never used. She asked for a job, and now leads platform security there. [Dark Reading, 2025](https://www.darkreading.com/cybersecurity-careers/capture-the-flag-leads-cybersecurity-careers)
- **Finn Lobsien**: He built examples with a company's own product for his application. They made room for him after the role was filled. [The unhinged application, 2024](https://userobsession.substack.com/p/the-unhinged-application-i-used-to)
- **atum47**: Rejected for having no public code, he posted his projects on Hacker News. A company in São Paulo hired him. [Hacker News, 2020](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=22050802)
- **Ryan Brown**: As an RIT student, his team's server-monitoring tool won a company's hackathon and earned him an interview. [RIT News, 2014](https://www.rit.edu/news/hackathons-help-students-get-jobs-make-difference)
- **Tim Park**: No internships and middling grades. Friends of friends forwarded his resume, and he got two offers. [freeCodeCamp, 2017](https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/how-i-got-my-first-developer-job-with-no-internships-straight-out-of-college-814d0eea1e4c/)
- **codeSTACKr**: He showed his boss a tool that automated slow manual work, and moved into a developer role. [My First Developer Job, DEV Community](https://dev.to/florinpop17/my-first-developer-job-30-stories-2j85)

